Modern Arsenal - modern military hardware for Terraria.
Designed to be played alongside the Calamity Mod (optional; detected at runtime).

v0.5.8
- Apache Guardian: an evasive loop. When it takes a burst of damage (from phase 2) or now and then from phase 3, it pulls
  up into a full 360-degree loop, dumps flares on the way in and takes 60% less damage until it comes out. 10 s cooldown.
- Drones resized against the Apache: the RQ-7B Shadow is about 1/5 of it (redrawn 1:1 so the detail stays), the MQ-1C
  Gray Eagle about half. Health: Gray Eagle 9000, Shadow 3000.
- Entrance: the drones now do a straight high-speed sweep past the Guardian (Eagle over the rotor, Shadow under the
  skids), then circle back into the fight.
- When the Shadow completes a lock, the Gray Eagle fires on the same lase.

v0.5.7
- New boss (test command for now: /apache guardian): the AH-64E Apache Guardian, with an MQ-1C Gray Eagle and an
  RQ-7B Shadow. Five phases. It fires Spike NLOS missiles: cold eject, then a steep climb out of sight and a dive onto
  you. The Shadow orbits over you and lases you; hold the lock for 2-2.5 s and the Guardian answers with 2-3 linked
  Spikes with tighter guidance. Break line of sight or hurt the Shadow to drop the lock. The Shadow also makes reckless
  ramming passes. The Gray Eagle works from your far side and drops Hellfires. The drones are bonus support: the Eagle
  cuts the Guardian's damage taken by 12%, the Shadow makes it 5% faster and brings the linked salvos.
- In the Guardian's entrance both drones trail it in, streak past it toward you, then bank round into formation.
- Drone lights done properly for a side view: port red / starboard green by facing, formation lights, white strobes,
  pulsing red beacons, white tail light (Common/Visuals/NavLightRig.cs).
- Missile smoke is now left in the world as separate puffs: it thins out from the launcher end first and lingers after
  the missile is gone, instead of a ribbon that stayed attached and vanished all at once. Launches throw a back-blast
  cloud out of the rear of the tube.

v0.5.6
- Apache entrance cutscene: it runs in from far off to one side, high and fast with its nose down, the Longbow radar
  pinging on the way in, then flares hard into a hover near you. The nose dips, the chin gun slews onto you, the nose
  sensor lases you with the lock tone, and the title card lands.
- Boss cutscenes no longer use black bars: the frame is drawn in the warning-banner style, red for the Apache and amber
  for the Humvee, with bevelled hazard stripes, a label plate and a running clock. It scales with any resolution.
  Mod config (Modern Arsenal: Visuals) can switch back to plain black bars. The frame, the title card and the warning
  banners are laid out on a 1080-high canvas scaled to the real screen, so they fill it edge to edge at any resolution
  and any UI scale setting.
- Apache: navigation lights (wing-tip position light, tail light, double-flash anti-collision beacon) and thin white
  vapour trails off the rotor tips and wing tip the whole time it flies, stronger at speed.
- Weapon effects: Hydra and Hellfire leave a smoke ribbon with a glowing exhaust; 12.7 mm (Humvee M2, red tracers) and
  30 mm (Apache M230) rounds get muzzle flashes, glowing tracers and impact sparks and dust; 30 mm HEDP bursts on impact.
- Fixed: rotor and engine loops (Apache, Humvee, Chinook, the airstrike and on-station Apaches) could keep playing after
  the boss was killed or left. Every loop is now owned by one system that stops it as soon as its owner is gone, and
  stops everything when you leave the world.

v0.5.5
- Air assault, reworked: the Chinook makes one long descending run-in and lets the Humvee go on the move. The platform
  slams down and skids, the tie-downs pop, the Chinook flares while the truck rolls off the front of the deck with its
  engine off, coasts, brakes to a stop, and cold-starts: the starter cranks with the headlights sagging on every stroke,
  it catches with a bark of black smoke and a lick of flame, the lights come up, and the title card lands on the catch.
- The Humvee has working headlights, a side marker and tail lights (brighter on the brakes), drawn as additive glow.
- An AH-64D passes far off in the background during the run-in.

v0.5.4
- The Chinook carries the Humvee on an olive-drab load platform, rigged the real way: reach pendant, apex fitting, four
  sling legs with chain ends on the platform shackles, and four ratchet tie-downs from the deck to the wheel hubs.
  The load trails and swings under the hook, the legs sag when the platform is on the ground.
- Airlift: the Chinook sets the empty platform down in front of the truck, the truck drives on, the tie-downs go on one
  by one, then the lift. After the drop the straps come off, the truck rolls off the deck, and the Chinook leaves with
  the empty platform swinging under it.

v0.5.3
- CH-47D Chinook (new pixel art, lit and weathered like the Apache): the Humvee now arrives by air assault. The Chinook
  swoops in with the truck on its sling, sets it down near you and leaves, with a short cutscene: letterbox, the camera
  rides along, title card. You can't be hurt or move while it plays.
- No more driving up into the air: when you hold a ledge the truck can't reach, or a wall blocks it, the crew calls the
  Chinook. It dives in, flares, hooks the truck, carries it over and drops it on your level (an amber HOSTILE AIRLIFT
  marker shows where). The gunner keeps firing while it hangs there. The load swings on the sling.
- Chinook lights: blinking position light (green or red by side), red double-flash beacons, tail light and a searchlight
  beam, drawn as additive glow. Two rotor loops, one per rotor head, beating against each other, plus the turbine whine.

v0.5.2
- Humvee has a full pattern set now instead of leaning on rams:
  M2 suppressive sweep: a fan of fire walked down across your area. Close in under the stream or get behind cover.
  Mk19 walked barrage: rounds land one after another along the ground, marching through you.
  Phase 2, doors off: it rolls in and the crew throws M67 frags out of the doorways. They bounce, land on
  platforms and cook off.
  Phase 2 fire mission: 60 mm mortars whistle down around you after a bracketing pair. A roof overhead stops them,
  and camping up high draws more of them.
- TOW is a TOW now: its own BGM-71 sprite, kicked out of the tube before the flight motor lights through the side
  nozzles, a flickering tail beacon, and guidance wires running back to the launcher. Kill the truck and the wires
  are cut.
- New Humvee alert: a two-note alert over the radio (squelch, tones, squelch) replaces the klaxon.

v0.5.1
- Humvee: pulling away, climbing and every ram now floor it: a hard rev, black smoke out of the exhaust, and the
  engine note climbs with the throttle instead of just the speed. Louder engine overall.
- Humvee warnings are its own: amber CONTACT banner with hazard tape and a two-tone klaxon, amber telegraphs, and a
  lower tracking tone for the TOW. The Apache keeps the red WARNING banner and RWR tone.
- Humvee has weight: the body squats when it pulls away, dives when it brakes and bounces on landings; screen shake
  on rams going past, hard landings, grenade bursts and the final blast.

v0.5.0
- New boss: M1151 Humvee, the first boss (before the Eye of Cthulhu). Summoned with a Road Flare, crafted from
  4 iron or lead bars, 10 Gel and 5 Torches at a work bench.
- A ground vehicle that never jumps. It drives on platforms, climbs up to your level nose-high, crawls over low
  walls, and when it can't reach you it pulls out of sight and comes in from the side.
- M2 .50 cal bursts, lobbed Mk19 grenades that burst on platforms too, and ground rams with a lane warning.
  Camping up high swaps the rams for more grenades.
- Destructible parts: turret (short, wild bursts and fewer grenades), both tires (it slides, brakes late and
  throws sparks off the rims) and, from phase 2, the engine (the hood blows off, it burns and loses speed).
- Phase 2 at half health: burnout, the doors get kicked off, and a TOW launcher goes up on the roof.
- Death: it burns out, then the fuel goes up and the truck comes apart.
- Boss theme: Armored Perimeter.
- Test command: /humvee [flare n | hp 1-100 | kill].
- Explosions spawned with 0 damage are effects only.

v0.4.4
- Apache flares are real decoys now. Each flare counts as an enemy, so homing weapons, minions and stray shots go
  for it instead of the gunship. They pop in one hit, drop nothing, heal nothing and burn out in a few seconds.
- From phase 3 the Apache throws a wide flare curtain toward you as it settles into a standoff.
- Explosions and destroyed parts puff vanilla smoke, so the blasts sit in the world like vanilla explosives.
- Boss parts run on a shared part system (groundwork for the next bosses). No change to how the Apache parts play.
- Humvee engine and M2 .50 cal sounds added for the upcoming Humvee boss.

v0.4.3
- Encrypted Field Radio is a straight summon again, framed as the enemy finding you: POSITION COMPROMISED banner,
  then the hostile Apache comes in.
- Laser Target Designator, right click: close air support terminal. Hold TRANSMIT to call a friendly AH-64D that
  hovers over you and works the nearest enemy with the M230, Hydra pairs and a homing Hellfire every 5 seconds.
  Costs 40 mana to call and 12 mana a second on station; it flies home when your mana runs out, or hold again to
  release it. The terminal can be dragged by its header bar.

v0.4.2
- Fire support terminal UI (moved to the Laser Target Designator in v0.4.3).
- M4A1 sounds: recorded AR-15 shots (three AUTO variants, a heavier SEMI shot), a selector click and brass casing clinks.
- M4A1 rebalanced: 11 damage. AUTO: 2.5 degree spread, 25% chance to save ammo. SEMI: 1.8x damage, +10% crit,
  10 armor penetration, 30% faster rounds, 12 ticks per shot.
- Test commands: /m4a1 or /apache m4 gives the M4A1 and an Endless Musket Pouch.

v0.4.1
- New weapon: M4A1 Carbine (pre-hardmode, after Skeletron). Crafted from a Minishark, Illegal Gun Parts, 12 iron or
  lead bars and 15 Bone at an anvil. Right click flips the selector between SEMI and AUTO.
- M4A1 shot animation: the bolt cycles in the ejection port, the gun kicks back and climbs, a muzzle flash shows at
  the flash hider, and brass casings fly out of the port, bounce off the ground and settle before fading.

v0.4.0
- Apache remake: every phase now opens with a sortie. The gunship climbs straight out of sight, strikes from above with
  radar-locked Hellfires (4 / 6 / 8 / 8, plus a Hydra salvo from phase 2) and dives back in along a shown lane; from
  phase 3 the dive goes straight through the player (phase 4: two passes). It can't be hit while it is up there.
- Hellfire guidance up about 20% (turn 0.044, top speed 15.5, seeker time 170 ticks); radar lock shots turn tighter too.
- build.txt restored (display name and version).

v0.3.2
- Long charge reworked Devourer-of-Gods style: goes 2600px out of sight, comes back from either side or diving from
  above, with blinking arrows on the screen edge while it is gone; more frequent from phase 2.
- Pilot radio and cockpit system messages rewritten as short English radio calls and caution codes (all languages).
- Fixed lofted Hellfires (volley and standoff) never guiding: the overshoot check tripped during the climb.

v0.3.1
- Apache: standoff strike (leaves the screen, then Hydras / Hellfires / long-range 30mm from out of sight, with warnings).
- Hellfire guidance +15%. Reworked engine fire (grows out of the engine, 2x2 pixel grid), half-size mini Apache sprites.

v0.3.0
- New drops: Mini Apache Remote (summon) and Laser Target Designator (off-screen Apache air support, with a rare gun run).
- Apache: long off-screen charges that dump flares, rockets peel off the short charge, Hydra salvos of up to 38 rockets,
  Hellfire volleys of up to 8, weighted shuffle-bag attack order.
- Wrecked systems now degrade instead of vanishing: jammed gun, misfiring pod, hand-flown radar lock.
- Part health scales with the airframe; parts are armored until later phases and ignored by homing weapons.
- Engine fire drawn from phase 3, gentler Hellfire guidance, custom arrival message, pilot/system chat colors.
- Fixed the rotor sound lingering after the fight and the boss theme losing to other mods' music.

v0.2.0
- Apache rework: four phases, randomized attack selection, new attacks (ram charge, Hydra rain,
  pop-up top-attack Hellfire, Longbow radar lock, strafing run) with on-screen warnings and path markers.
- Destructible systems: M230 gun, rocket pod, Longbow radar and tail rotor each have their own health.
- Progressive damage: smoke, sparks, engine fire, cracked canopy, and a crash sequence on death.
- Fixed flares firing endlessly below 25% health.
- Boss theme added.

v0.1.0
- Boss: AH-64D Apache (post-Golem). Summoned with the Encrypted Field Radio.

